    "comment": "Review waived: section 12 was re-reviewed and its findings answered; this node continues the bulk reprocess that ssfms-reprocess-bulk-1 began (54 small categories, 733 signals; rates 24 signals per minute on tiny catalogues and 122 per minute on coil instrumentation). Work only on the assigned categories, passing --category on every command so no run claims another node's signals; other bulk nodes run in parallel on different categories. Reset with: imas-codex discover jt-60sa --only signals --scan-only --reset-to discovered --category <cats> (or --focus <ids>), once per scope; enrich with --flush and the same scope, without --reset-to, under -t 9 per pass, repeating until the scope has none at discovered. Do not run backfill_signal_roles: a single facility-wide role pass follows the last bulk node. Do not write reprocess.html or reprocess-progress.json; record only in your own two files. Runs in place on the fleet allocation; keep each command in the foreground under 10 minutes and write your progress file after every scope. First finish b260008: 13 of its signals were left at discovered by ssfms-reprocess-bulk-2; enrich them with --flush --category b260008 and no reset, before any new scope. b260008's other 2,946 signals are already reprocessed, so never reset b260008 again. Reset no more than about 800 signals in one scope: ssfms-reprocess-bulk-2 reset all 2,959 of b260008 at once and left 13 at discovered when its time ran out.",
